Z||000004||RNGCRSH||02-22-2001||12:32 AM||||I'm sure you have burped the coolant system. If not then do that. You might also want to flush the Radiator/make sure there are no obstructions in the coolsnt lines. Have you checked the water Pump? <P>and just for kicks, Check the Fan  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000005||sqoach||02-22-2001||12:54 AM||||ok, i'm not as mad now. as for the smartasses that replied, thanks  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif"><BR>at least you made me laugh  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>ok, i KNOW it's not the fan, cuz the fan works. new fan motor, new relay. turn on a/c, fan works. what i don't know is if the fan switch works. but, my temp never gets to the stock switch-on temp for it to turn on. when it does get that high, it goes up really fast and overheats. so, even if the fan switch worked, there's no way it could cool it down enough cuz the temp rises too fast.<P>with that said, what the hell do i do? i'm not finding any coolant in my oil, and my coolant looks normal. i've burped the system a million times. it seems to not overheat for a while after i burp it, but then it happens again. i can't figure it out. i thought maybe there's a leak somewhere, but i figured i would see little drops of coolant where i park, which i don't see.<P>maybe i will invest in a honda, cuz this is stressing the hell outta me. bastard, wouldn't you get stressed out if the only vehicle you had to drive kept overheating, and it's been doing it for a long time, and you've tried everything you can think of, and you're poor and don't have money to take it somewhere?<P>aren't fieros great  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
